  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Foster entrepreneurial learning and the creation of MSMEs for young graduates in Libya</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Ministry of Economy and Industry in Libya requested UNIDO&apos;s support to initiate and implement an entrepreneurship programme for youth in Libya (Ministry&apos;s letter of 12 Sept 2017).  UNIDO has been discussing with the HP Foundation, HP Inc. and GIZ a partnership initiative to foster entrepreneurial learning for young graduates in Libya based on HP&apos;s Learning Initiative for Entrepreneurs (HP LIFE),  applied in UNIDO&apos;s youth employment project in Tunisia (SAP 120357),  combined with GIZ&apos; Competency-based economies through formation of enterprise (CEFE) programme. The initiative will be implemented within the South-South Cooperation scheme and aligned to the United Nations Strategic Framework (UNSF) for Libya.</narrative>
  </description>
